{"content":"Implemented the fix for repositories containing a `.*` ignore pattern.\n\n### Changes\n- Prevented ignore matchers from evaluating the traversal root (`\".\"`) in:\n  - `ListDirectory`, used by file completion.\n  - `GlobWithDoubleStar`, the glob fallback implementation.\n- Descendant files and directories are still evaluated normally, so hidden files remain ignored.\n- Added a regression test verifying that:\n  - Regular files are returned with `.*` in `.gitignore`.\n  - Hidden files remain excluded.\n  - Both directory listing and glob traversal behave correctly.\n\n### Verification\nPerformed a final source-level review of all modified files. Automated verification was attempted, but the environment could not execute `gofmt` (`execvp: No such file or directory`), and fail-fast canceled the focused `go test ./internal/fsext` step before it ran. No alternative tooling or network access was attempted.","type":"text"}
